    "intro": "Starting a heating, ventilation and air conditioning firm, or setting up as a heating engineer? This **HVAC business name generator** has catchy and funny names, classic family names, professional and modern ones, plus names from your town or first name.",
    "sections": [],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do I check an HVAC business name is free?",
        "answer": "Press <strong>Check</strong> next to any name to see if it's free as a company, a domain and a social media handle. Then make sure: in the UK, search Companies House and the UK IPO trade mark register; in the US, search your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search. A quick map search for the name in your area helps too."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are some catchy HVAC company names?",
        "answer": "Catchy HVAC names play on comfort and temperature: <em>Keep Your Cool HVAC</em>, <em>Degrees of Comfort</em>, <em>Goldilocks Heating & Air</em> or <em>Pilot Light Heating & Cooling</em>. In the UK, &ldquo;Heating & Air Conditioning&rdquo; or &ldquo;Heating Engineers&rdquo; reads more naturally than HVAC. Choose <strong>Catchy</strong> in the Style menu for more."
      }
    ]
